        "input": {
          "instructions": "Clear, measured, and instructor-ready.",
          "text": "A professional design review closes the loop with measurable evidence. For performance, inspect zero-load latency, saturation throughput, and tail latency. For energy, separate router, buffer, link, and radio costs. For resilience, ask what happens when a link, router, or wireless channel fails, and whether packets can reroute without deadlock. A hybrid design is valuable only when its benefits survive realistic traffic and faults. The transferable lesson is systems thinking: architecture, communication, workload, and reliability are coupled, so every optimization must be evaluated end to end."
        },
